    "result_text": "The build passes \u2014 the target test is green and the full suite (including the JaCoCo coverage gate) succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist by following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (a `Require<Rule>` guard step that throws a checked escalation handled into a 400), mirroring the existing `NormalizeOwnerEmail`/`InvalidEmailException` pattern.\n\nNew files:\n- `rest/function/owner/DisposableEmailDomains.java` \u2014 package-private helper holding the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) and a case-insensitive domain check.\n- `rest/function/owner/RequireEmailNotDisposable.java` \u2014 guard step; skips blank emails, throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` for a blocked domain.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the offending value.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, matching the existing email/telephone handlers.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\nWiring: inserted a `disposableEmail` step after the `email` (normalize) step in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, so it runs after normalization (lower-cased, blanks already skipped) and under the same transaction governance.\n\nBehavior notes:\n- Blank/absent emails are still allowed (consistent with `NormalizeOwnerEmail`).\n- Applies to both create and update endpoints.\n- The check runs after email normalization, so mixed-case domains are still caught.",
